775,"lo":-80.186,"d":867,"ds":"Bayfront Park is a 32-acre (13 ha) public, urban park in the Central Business District of Downtown Miami, Florida on Biscayne Bay.","wpu":"Bayfront Park","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Bayfront_Plaza_2020.jpg/960px-Bayfront_Plaza_2020.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"InterContinental Miami","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":25.772419,"lo":-80.185373,"d":964,"ds":"The InterContinental Miami is a luxury hotel in Downtown Miami, Florida near Bayfront Park. Opened in 1983, it is owned by Strategic Hotels & Resorts and operated by IHG Hotels & Resorts as part of its InterContinental portfolio.","wpu":"InterContinental Miami","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Hotel_Intercontinental_Miami_20100707.jpg/960px-Hotel_Intercontinental_Miami_20100707.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Vizcayne","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":25.776733,"lo":-80.188836,"d":1094,"ds":"Vizcayne (formerly known as \"Everglades on the Bay\") is an urban development in the City of Miami, Florida. It is located in northeastern Downtown Miami and consists of two residential skyscrapers, North Tower and the South Tower as well as a retail center. The buildings were topped out (reached full height) in 2007, and were completed in early 2008.","wpu":"Vizcayne","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0d/Everglades_on_the_Bay_north_tower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Asia (Miami)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":25.769349,"lo":-80.185631,"d":1228,"ds":"Asia is a residential skyscraper on Brickell Key in the Brickell district of Downtown Miami, Florida, United States. The tower rises 483 feet (147 m), with 36 floors. Asia was topped out in mid-2007, and was completed structurally in January 2008.","wpu":"Asia (Miami)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Asia_tower.jpg/960px-Asia_tower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Marinablue","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":25.782222,"lo":-80.189722,"d":1264,"ds":"MarinaBlue, also known as Marina Blue, is a skyscraper in Miami, Florida, United States. It is located in northeastern Downtown, on Biscayne Bay along the west side of Biscayne Boulevard. The tower was one of the first buildings in Park West to be completed.","wpu":"Marinablue","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/MarinaBlue%2C_June_2015.jpg/960px-MarinaBlue%2C_June_2015.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Aston Martin Residences","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":25.77077,"lo":-80.18785,"d":1272,"ds":"Aston Martin Residences is a 66-story skyscraper in Miami, Florida, United States, located in Downtown Miami along the Miami River and Biscayne Bay. The building is the third-tallest in Miami and the state of Florida, it features a helipad on the roof and a full-service marina that can accommodate superyachts. The building contains 391 residences, with 99% of those residences have been sold as of May 6, 2024.","wpu":"Aston Martin Residences","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Aston_Martin_Residences_Downtown_Miami_31_December_2023.jpg/960px-Aston_Martin_Residences_Downtown_Miami_31_December_2023.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Olympia Theater (Miami)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":25.7742,"lo":-80.190517,"d":1322,"ds":"The Olympia Theater is a theater located in Miami, Florida. Designed by John Eberson in his famed atmospheric style, the theater opened in 1926. Throughout its history, the venue has served as a movie theater, concert venue and performing arts center.","wpu":"Olympia Theater (Miami)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Olympia_Theatre_Miami_exterior_2016.jpg/960px-Olympia_Theatre_Miami_exterior_2016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Carbonell Condominium","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":25.76925,"lo":-80.18695,"d":1322,"ds":"Carbonell Condominium is a residential high-rise building located in the Brickell neighborhood of Miami, Florida. The tower is one of the tallest buildings located on Brickell Key, a small island located due east of Brickell at the mouth of the Miami River in Biscayne Bay. Standing at 410 feet (125 metres), the building is currently tied with Two Tequesta Point as the 88th-tallest building in the city.","wpu":"Carbonell Condominium","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Carbonell_condo.png/960px-Carbonell_condo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Dodge Island","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":25.772378,"lo":-80.166206,"d":1336,"ds":"Dodge Island is an artificial island near downtown Miami, Florida, United States. The Port of Miami is located on, what was, Dodge, Lummus and Sam Islands, and has berths for both cruise and cargo ships. The original and much smaller Dodge Island was created during the dredging of Government Cut in the early 1900s.","wpu":"Dodge Island","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/7f/Port_of_Miami_Florida.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"MacArthur Causeway","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":25.777778,"lo":-80.164444,"d":1357,"ds":"The General Douglas MacArthur Causeway is a six-lane causeway that connects Downtown Miami to South Beach via Biscayne Bay in Miami-Dade County. The highway is the singular roadway connecting the mainland and beaches to Watson Island and the bay neighborhoods of Palm Island, Hibiscus Island, and Star Island. The MacArthur Causeway carries State Road A1A over the Biscayne Bay via a girder bridge.","wpu":"MacArthur Causeway","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Watson_Island.png/960px-Watson_Island.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Shoreland Arcade","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":25.775154,"lo":-80.19131,"d":1369,"ds":"The Shoreland Arcade (also known as the Dade Federal Savings) is a historic site in Miami, Florida. It is located at 120 Northeast 1st Street. On January 4, 1989, it was added to the U.S. National Register of Historic Places.","wpu":"Shoreland Arcade","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Miami_FL_Downtown_HD_Shoreland_Arcade01.jpg/960px-Miami_FL_Downtown_HD_Shoreland_Arcade01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Dupont Plaza Hotel (Miami)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":25.770572,"lo":-80.189136,"d":1387,"ds":"The Dupont Plaza Hotel was a major hotel in downtown Miami, Florida from 1957 until 2004. It occupied a section of the former site of the Royal Palm Hotel. The Dupont Plaza Hotel was the first major hotel of its generation built in downtown Miami since the collapse of the tourist boom in 1926.","wpu":"Dupont Plaza Hotel (Miami)","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/56/Dupont_Plaza_Hotel_Miami.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"I-395 Signature Bridge","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":25.78593,"lo":-80.18909,"d":1417,"ds":"The Interstate-395 Signature Overpass (also referred to as The Fountain) is an ongoing construction project on the I-395/SR-836/I-95 Midtown Interchange in downtown Miami, Florida. The overpass was designed by Donald MacDonald architects, led by the Archer-Western-de Moya Group. The Florida Department of Transportation (FDOT) and Miami-Dade Expressway Authority are the current overseers of the project.","wpu":"I-395 Signature Bridge","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/91/I-395_Signature_Bridge_Rendering.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Hahn Building","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":25.775947,"lo":-80.192036,"d":1423,"ds":"The Hahn Building is a historic site in Miami, Florida, United States. It is located at 140 Northeast 1st Avenue. On January 4, 1989, it was added to the U.S. National Register of Historic Places.","wpu":"Hahn Building","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/HahnBuilding.jpg/960px-HahnBuilding.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Miami Tower","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":25.772,"lo":-80.1912,"d":1480,"ds":"The Miami Tower (previously known as CenTrust Tower and Bank of America Tower) is a 47-story, landmark office skyscraper in Miami, Florida, United States. It is located in central Downtown. It is currently the 21st tallest building in Miami and Florida.","wpu":"Miami Tower","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Bank_of_America_Miami_20100206.jpg/960px-Bank_of_America_Miami_20100206.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Miami is a coastal city in the southeast portion of the U.S. state of Florida. It is the second-most populous city proper in Florida, with a population of 442,241 at the 2020 census. The Miami metropolitan area in South Florida has an estimated 6.39 million residents, ranking as the fifth-largest metropolitan area in the Southeast and eighth-largest metropolitan area in the United States.","wpu":"Miami","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Miami%2C_Florida%2C_Skyline_4.jpg/960px-Miami%2C_Florida%2C_Skyline_4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}